# pipeline/{%slug%}

Python side of the `{%slug%}` package (kinds: {%kindsCsv%}). Scaffolded by `atlas new model {%slug%}` on {%today%}.
The page code lives in `site/src/lib/explainers/{%slug%}/`; notes go in `notes/{%slug%}.md`.

Run everything through the CLI from `site/` (or a lane's `site/`): it uses the configured Python
(`site/scripts/atlas/atlas.config.local.json`, else `python` on PATH) and sets `PYTHONPATH=<repo>/pipeline`,
`ATLAS_SITE` and `ATLAS_ROOT`, so files land in the right site even inside a lane.

| File | What it does | Run |
|---|---|---|
{%#trace%}
| `model.py` | the PyTorch model (train it with a fixed seed; save `runs/<run>/best.pt`) | `npm run atlas -- py pipeline/{%slug%}/model.py` (smoke test) |
| `export.py` | `describe()` + `ak.export_model(...)`: spec.json, weights.bin, reference.json | `npm run atlas -- export {%slug%}` |
{%/trace%}
{%#train%}
| `twin.py` | the PyTorch fp64 twin of the TS trainer (`build(cfg)`, `loss(model, batch, cfg)`) | `npm run atlas -- parity {%slug%}` |
{%/train%}
{%#process%}
| `reference.py` | an independent Python run of the TS process (same rng, same frames) | `npm run atlas -- run {%slug%} run --save`, then `npm run atlas -- py pipeline/{%slug%}/reference.py` |
{%/process%}

Rules: CPU only and TF32 off for references (importing `atlas_kit` does it; AK102 otherwise). No new downloads without
the user's OK. Each file <= 5 MB, each model <= 15 MB (AK105). Every dataset or ported code goes into `credits` in
`explainer.ts`.
